WEBVTT

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.750
Low battery?

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.200
Impossible.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.000
The newly discovered body
 has yet to be identified.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.120
It's the tenth corpse
 since the case came to light.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.200
Last month, the Radical Superhuman
 Revolutionary Force took hostages.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.450
They were suppressed by
 the National Public Security Force.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:34.290
Since then, bodies seemingly of the
 Revolutionary Force have been found.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.040
The hostage case
 is taking on a new turn.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.160
Jiro Hitoyoshi.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.330
Finally got curry flavor.
 They're sold out everywhere.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.120
Why are you here?

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.290
What are you doing? What for?

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.290
Why'd you pull the plug?

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:52.910
It's time for the news.
 Don't hog the outlets.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.830
It's for home use.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.080
Hurry up and get out.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.750
Why the cold shoulder? We're friends.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.660
Friends? You robbed me of Megasshin.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.330
It's been less than 2 weeks.
 And you're a friend?

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.620
If only I had Megasshin.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.580
It wouldn't have been like this?

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:14.830
How dare you!

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.160
Hungry, huh?

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.330
Hey, Mr. Shiba.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.200
You were with
 the Revolutionary Force, right?

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.750
Paranoia is the greatest enemy.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.730
As immature superhumans gathered,
 we became unable to trust.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.250
Yet, you wanted to protect them.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:39.490
Don't act a stranger.
 You and I are the same.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.290
Be prepared.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.700
The war for justice
 has already started.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.000
(March, the 47th of Shinka Era
 Yoyogi)

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.790
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.930
This world that you couldn't forgive
 is such a beautiful place

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:10.230
Are you saying everything that
 bears sadness is evil?

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:15.570
Even if the children crumble
 with guns of reality pointed at them

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.660
I am me and nothing else

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.660
I gain through gunpoint

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.790
Ready to fight

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.700
I'll rise like the break of dawn

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.370
I save them for the final day

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.370
Dream of the world
 for me and "fantasia"

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.950
It's time to go
 Unshaken mind

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.700
Change the world

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.200
I shake off my wavering gaze

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.910
And find my beloved justice

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.370
I live for the tomorrow
 that is unspoken of

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.080
Amidst evanescence and pain

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.700
Only the break of day drives me on

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.870
Until the day
 everything has returned

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.910
I face such horror tonight

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.470
(The Superhumans of November)

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.720
(October, the 46th of Shinka Era
 Matsumoto)

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.660
Okay. Superhumans, fight.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.410
I wish he'd say something else.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:34.790
Yumihiko. I'm sorry, you've decided
 to go by the name Daitetsu-boy, right?

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.750
Either's fine.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.750
Are you okay?

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.830
Were you the kind that always
 got carsick during school trips?

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.040
- My head hurts.
 - Take it off.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.790
I can't.
 This is an important experiment.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.080
Gear test for
 superhuman security measures.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.920
Attack according to plan.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.120
I've already forgotten the plan.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.040
I'm going ahead and ending this.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.580
Miss Kikko, take Yumihiko for me.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.750
Be happy and go on...

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:15.400
I...

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:16.830
I...

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.370
I didn't punch him that hard.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.080
Remember what
 today's training is for.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.250
The Superhuman Bureau and
 civil superhuman security measures.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.120
Whenever there's action,

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.580
they'll come under the command of
 the National Public Security Force.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.380
Superhumans are
 no longer to be protected.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.120
They're dangerous criminals.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.910
I don't want to fight
 the students anymore.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.830
But it's true that
 they're getting radical.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.000
They're losing public support.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.230
Are you fine with it, Mr. Jaguar?

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:01.370
Just look at how helpless the police
 are when we counted on them.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.330
Not good.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:08.910
Alxe uses the energy of the rider
 to increase its mobility time.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.410
Mr. Shiba sustains a back-flow.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.830
No excuses.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:16.160
To protect this country,
 the superhumans must be...

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.540
Killed?

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:27.040
You can capture them all you want,
 but they'll just keep appearing.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.700
They just want their freedom.

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.220
Our mission is to arrest criminals.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.370
But killing superhumans is...

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.330
Raito Shiba?

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.620
Don't touch me!

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.410
Have you gone nuts?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.250
Just look at them.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.500
Let them be.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:53.950
The police and the army
 have always hated each other.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.080
A flying saucer?

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.080
Not OK. What's gotten into you?

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.790
You're the protectors of this planet.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.120
It's wrong for you to fight.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:13.720
Who are you?

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.870
Forgive me.
 It's hard to explain, so...

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.620
How about this?

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.750
An Android Warrior from space?
 This is interesting.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:32.620
He's from the Peace Federation
 of seventy-some intelligent species.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.250
Even better. I've heard rumors.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:38.250
My name is Yusei Washizu.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.500
I've integrated the federation's will.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.830
I was made mainly
 for pursuing criminals.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.250
He wants our help to arrest
 a criminal that's hiding in Earth.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.910
A joint transborder investigation.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.750
Then why don't you detectives do it?

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.480
A holograph. And a precise one too.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.750
- We can't see, Professor.
 - Hey.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.360
I've seen that.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.450
An "S" Planetarian.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:10.040
"S" Planetarians had been making
 black holes all around the galaxy.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:14.000
And many solar systems disappeared.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:18.000
What you call Scorpio X1
 is a trace of one of them.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:22.250
The Federation fought them
 for millions of years.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.540
And finally defeated them.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:28.200
Yet, some remnants had been
 hiding out on this planet.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:31.290
Time sure flows differently
 for aliens.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.590
The one you're after...

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.870
Was defeated 5 years ago.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:40.000
By the being you call Grosse Augen.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:44.440
There's a possibility that
 he also was a runaway.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.750
But that's irrelevant to my mission.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:50.620
The "S" Planetarian
 is still living on this planet.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:55.000
This is footage from 6 months ago
 at an area called Shinjuku.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.750
I have to go grocery shopping.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:07:59.790
Good day.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.120
- Hoshino?
 - Kikko-chan?

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.330
I told you we should've reported it.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.580
I warned you there was
 nothing to be gained.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.540
And now...

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.500
To the other side of the galaxy.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:25.540
Fly away.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:30.400
Superhuman Detective Raito.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.250
Stop calling me that.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:36.790
We're finally prepared to capture
 the "S" Planetarian.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.450
It's all thanks to you.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.910
Don't be shy.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:42.580
Feel free to call me Galaxy Captain.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.170
Why Captain?

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:48.170
A man resembling Akira Shirota
 was seen outside the park.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.910
Shirota had once coexisted
 with Grosse Augen.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.930
To think he'd fused with
 an "S" Planetarian.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:59.250
Who is this Jiro Hitoyoshi
 who secretly directed this?

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.870
A former Bureau guy.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.910
But now he's their enemy.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.940
Whatever can he be thinking?

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.410
To join forces with
 a dangerous "S" Planetarian.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.330
I...

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.870
I cannot understand.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:14.750
No, I think I can.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:18.410
He always wanted to
 protect superhumans.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.040
He believed
 in righteous superhumans.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:24.200
But the Bureau went against that,
 and now fights superhumans.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.460
You don't understand... You shouldn't.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:28.750
What did you say?

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:32.080
Space, Earth...
 There's only one justice.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.910
Crime cannot be forgiven.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.830
If superhumans are against the law,

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:39.330
a righteous superhuman
 is a contradiction.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.450
Yeah, you're right.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.250
We're both detectives.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.250
I empathize with you.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:53.080
For Okinawa's return,
 the U.S. Army and Self Defense Forces

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.250
are conspiring about
 an artificial island.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:10:00.250
This could be a newer version
 of the Ogasawara superhuman lab.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:05.200
A student rally against the treaty
 concerning Okinawa continues.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:06.870
What's that?

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:15.040
It's a beast found a few years ago
 in Okinawa.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.760
If the artificial island is made,
 they'll lose their habitat.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.640
They brought it to Tokyo?

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.830
It's the same for beasts
 and superhumans.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:27.310
They shouldn't be suppressed by
 laws and the Bureau.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.830
What the...

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.830
It's mad since it was forced to come.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.620
This could get dangerous.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:45.120
Hey, get the guy
 who brought the beast.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.080
It's a beast.
 The trend has died down, but...

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:55.040
Hurry, run. Leave it to the Bureau.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:56.790
Bureau?

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:01.410
Mr. Shirota, we're just here to
 watch the Bureau.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.620
But the students.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:15.000
So it's true that
 Grosse Augen is back.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:18.000
But he's different. The color too.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:20.080
He probably just feels like it.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.870
Long time no see, Jiro.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:23.910
That hurts.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.910
You promised never to see
 Kikko Hoshino.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.330
She saw me on the train.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.870
But I won't see her again.
 We're enemies.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.170
Then just come back to me.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:41.330
Emi. I'm beginning to see
 your real objective.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:45.160
The Bureau set this up today, right?

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.830
Make the beast go wild
 and blame the students?

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.080
You're too naive, Jiro.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.620
Kikai?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:05.080
I will not allow you
 to go back to being human.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.450
"S" Planetarian.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:10.830
Think you're protecting humans
 from evil superhumans?

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:14.200
But your body is that of a criminal.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.200
After Mr. Shirota?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.160
And you're using students as bait.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.120
You're used to it. The Bureau's ways.

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:25.220
The chief wouldn't have been so dirty.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.250
It's Raito in the Kikai.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.160
And he hated it so much.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.830
He said the Bureau was shady.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:36.250
Jiro.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.000
It's fine.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.750
He's ours either way.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.330
Jiro. You're not coming?

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.700
You can drink?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:57.370
Alcohol is broken down in my body
 to create energy and to disinfect.

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:59.040
But that's too much.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.160
And you, Mr. Galaxy Union?

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.830
This vinegared octopus
 is very interesting.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:06.090
And sliced squid.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.410
Octopus and squid?
 You like alien-like things, huh?

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:13.790
Come on, those are Martians.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.580
I died. A long time ago.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:20.230
So your memory was transferred
 to that body?

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.290
A mysterious scientist
 performed the operation.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.580
That's what they told me.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.450
But I found out who he was
 3 years ago.

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:31.370
That Ogasawara lab doctor, right?

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:36.250
Ones who experimented on
 superhumans with the U.S.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:39.250
So my body was
 just another experiment.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.120
For military use of superhumans.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:44.470
Originally the wartime research
 of Type A and Type B.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:48.160
I've died once.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:51.160
That's why I wanted to be more human.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:55.250
To protect the law as a human.
 To be right as a superhuman.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.060
Whether you're a righteous
 superhuman is irrelevant.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:02.580
No matter what powers one has,
 a criminal is evil.

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.660
Righteous superhumans don't exist.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:09.500
Only freaks that cause trouble
 or will cause trouble.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.080
Freaks, huh?

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.830
Forgive me.

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.500
You're right.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:25.710
A machine like me
 shouldn't lose my way.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.250
You're not to blame.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:31.750
Nowadays, we suppress superhumans
 with even the slightest suspicion.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.700
Not just arrest, but at times...

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:37.000
Looks like you need some new parts.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:40.870
Luckily, we seem to
 use compatible parts.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:43.540
After the execution,
 I'll give you my spares.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:44.750
Execution?

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:49.160
Yes. To make an example out of
 the "S" Planetarian.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.490
I shall do a public execution.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.290
You're the one calling me?

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:09.010
The "S" Planetarian left a bit of
 energy, so I can speak.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:14.330
I'm sorry, but that's
 a space criminal's body.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:18.660
I realize that if you part
 with that, you'll die.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:21.580
I gave my life to Grosse Augen.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.910
I told you I have no regrets.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:26.400
But someone wants to see you.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:29.910
Jiro Senpai?

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.620
He wants to see you alone.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:41.370
You, ghost.
 Glad you're here, stop Hoshinoko.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.540
I'm your teacher, you know.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:45.880
Meteortail.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:56.330
The airport in Chofu?

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.290
Why here?

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.580
It's hardly used
 due to the Okinawa return.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.750
So no casualties if something happens.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.040
Senpai.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.320
Sorry, Kikko.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.330
How could you?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.910
I'm here, Mr. Shirota.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:29.410
Is this the old Ikuta Lab?

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:31.380
Equus.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.260
So he used Akira Shirota as bait
 to get Equus back?

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.410
He's learned a few dirty tricks.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.500
My seal is broken.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:46.370
But the monster in Jiro
 is under control.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.040
Why?

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.120
A Fumer.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:50.370
A Fumer?

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:52.580
A gas-like species.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:57.410
They find developing civilizations
 and intervene as leaders and reign.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:59.620
They think they're gods.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.580
They've even come here...

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.120
Does that mean...

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:06.380
The missing chief is protecting Jiro?

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:07.880
Alxe!

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.620
Jiro Hitoyoshi.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.250
Mr. Shiba.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.330
You're in the Bureau now?

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:26.650
You're under arrest.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.830
Your dream has come true.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:31.000
All superhumans are criminals now.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.400
Happy now?

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.660
Mr. Shiba.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.660
He's been acting strange.

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.950
Or rather,
 he was beginning to be normal.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:43.250
What do you mean?

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:48.000
That detective believed that
 he could be a righteous existence.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.580
That's why he hated
 criminal superhumans excessively.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:55.660
That was how he tried to be human.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:56.700
But now...

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:59.620
Machines can't bear inconsistencies.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.950
Superhuman detective.
 Looks like you need repairs.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:10.870
Woah!

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:13.190
That's Mr. Shiba's.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:21.620
Jiro.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.410
He's a traitor.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:26.330
But you can't let
 a Space Sheriff kill him.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.090
Get out of my way.

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:38.090
He's way more dangerous
 than "S" Planetarians.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:41.850
Fumers take over intelligent minds
 and control their minds.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:44.250
So that's what Mr. Akita was.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.750
That's why Jiro...

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:48.870
But Jiro-san is still
 important to me.

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:50.850
At least say "to us".

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:53.610
You're too childish to speak justice.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.450
Oh no. At this rate...

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:03.660
It's too late.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:28.080
He's controlled by Fumers,
 but not completely.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.200
You shouldn't be here.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:35.700
Jiro!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.500
Mr. Shiba?

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.380
What have I done?

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:57.200
I know.

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:58.580
I knew.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:00.080
I should've known.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:01.590
What I should've done.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:04.340
The "S" Planetarian is a criminal.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.600
Jiro protects even criminals.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.500
Both are my enemies.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:12.580
I knew that.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:14.200
I want to be cured.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:16.750
I will be cured.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.120
I'm broken.

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:21.870
Broken.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:25.750
I want to do right.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.040
Don't, Mr. Shiba.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.580
You are the old me.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.410
Back when I was sure of myself.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:40.790
Give it to me.

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:44.340
As long as I have this...

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:48.600
He was the most decent human
 amongst all of us.

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.080
Hitoyoshi.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:56.370
Senpai!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.830
I'm glad I'd kept it clean for him.

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:21.840
I finally understand.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:24.700
What the right thing is.

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:27.140
What I should do.

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:30.250
By inheriting that android's part,

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:32.500
I became a righteous being again.

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:36.910
But the police tried to
 dispose of me as broken.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:41.410
I am justice.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.540
If I were considered to be wrong,

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:46.000
those who say so are wrong.

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:48.830
So I turned my back on the nation.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.160
Am I wrong?

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.910
I broke Washizu.

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:56.660
The one who was like the old me.

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:58.700
I broke him.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:01.950
Was that wrong too?

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.830
And now...

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:10.450
To outer space...

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.390
And now...

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:17.890
You're a superhuman too.

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:20.700
So I will protect you.

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:23.830
Fly away...

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:40.870
In this age where
 ideals are just a fantasy

00:22:41.870 --> 00:22:48.290
Where are you going to
 reach out to?

00:22:48.330 --> 00:22:50.870
Alone by yourself

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:52.790
Always

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:54.750
Always

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:57.700
With somebody's justice

00:22:58.370 --> 00:23:05.940
You're suffering to protect what?

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:10.490
If you're still captured...

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:12.040
I can't hold you

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:16.080
On these streets without any signs...

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:20.330
A child is crying

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:27.510
Ideals are just a toy, anyway

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:34.660
But you still reach out your hands

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:42.080
Righteous heroes are probably
 just beyond your reach

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:48.540
I don't mind
 I just want to keep watching...

00:23:49.700 --> 00:23:52.370
Just that one person

00:23:57.410 --> 00:23:59.750
My love was crushed
 and crumbled away.

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:04.250
Now that they're stardust, maybe I'll
 go chase them to Andromeda's end.

00:24:04.290 --> 00:24:07.000
Who said home has to be Earth?

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:10.830
The last stage for the Angel Stars.
 Time to say goodbye to the Angels.
